    <item>
      <title>Day 1 - Week 1</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-1/dia-1/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-1/dia-1/</guid>
      <description>&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-learning-objectives&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;🎯 Learning Objectives &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-learning-objectives&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At the end of the class, you will be able to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Pronounce and spell the English alphabet correctly.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Recognize and say numbers from &lt;strong&gt;0 to 1,000,000&lt;/strong&gt; including teen/ten differences and &lt;strong&gt;TH sounds&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Use titles like &lt;strong&gt;Mr., Mrs., Ms.&lt;/strong&gt; properly.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Apply basic &lt;strong&gt;connected speech&lt;/strong&gt; rules for natural pronunciation.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-introduction&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;📖 Introduction &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-introduction&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Today you will pronounce and spell words correctly following the &lt;strong&gt;Alphabet&lt;/strong&gt; and the &lt;strong&gt;Military Phonetic Alphabet&lt;/strong&gt;. Besides, you will recognize and write numbers from &lt;strong&gt;1 to 1,000,000&lt;/strong&gt;. You will be able to understand the differences of &lt;strong&gt;teen/ten&lt;/strong&gt; and practice the &lt;strong&gt;TH sound&lt;/strong&gt;. Finally, you will learn how to use &lt;strong&gt;titles&lt;/strong&gt; properly and address people in a polite manner. You will also learn two basic rules of &lt;strong&gt;connected speech&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Day 1 - Week 1</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/elementary/semana-1/el-week1-day1/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/elementary/semana-1/el-week1-day1/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;temas-del-día&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Temas del Día &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#temas-del-d%c3%ada&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Magic Questions and Phrases&lt;/strong&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Greetings&lt;/strong&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Definite and Infinite Articles&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;objetivos-del-aprendizaje&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Objetivos del aprendizaje &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#objetivos-del-aprendizaje&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h4 id=&#34;al-finalizar-esta-clase-serás-capaz-de&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Al finalizar esta clase, serás capaz de:&lt;/em&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#al-finalizar-esta-clase-ser%c3%a1s-capaz-de&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1.&lt;/strong&gt; Utilizar exclusivamente el idioma inglés en el salón de clases mediante el uso constante de frases y preguntas básicas/comunes.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Day 1 - Week 2</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-2/dia-1/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-2/dia-1/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;-learning-objectives&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;🎯 Learning Objectives &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-learning-objectives&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At the end of the class, you will be able to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Review &lt;strong&gt;class rules&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;magic questions&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Simple Present&lt;/strong&gt; tense thoroughly.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Learn &lt;strong&gt;regular vs. irregular Simple Past&lt;/strong&gt; verbs.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Focus on &lt;strong&gt;ED ending pronunciation&lt;/strong&gt; and memorize &lt;strong&gt;80 common verbs&lt;/strong&gt; for storytelling and past events.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-introduction&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;📖 Introduction &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-introduction&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Today you will reinforce &lt;strong&gt;Week 1 foundations&lt;/strong&gt; while introducing &lt;strong&gt;Simple Past&lt;/strong&gt; verbs. As A1 students, you must follow the class rules and use the &lt;strong&gt;magic questions&lt;/strong&gt; for English-only participation. Finally, you will memorize past tense verbs to describe yesterday&amp;rsquo;s actions or experiences.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Day 1 - Week 2</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/elementary/semana-2/el-week2-day1/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/elementary/semana-2/el-week2-day1/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;temas-del-día&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Temas del Día &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#temas-del-d%c3%ada&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simple Present Rules and Uses&lt;/strong&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;3rd Person Singular Rule&lt;/strong&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Simple Present Time Expressions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;objetivos-del-aprendizaje&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Objetivos del aprendizaje: &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#objetivos-del-aprendizaje&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h4 id=&#34;al-finalizar-esta-clase-serás-capaz-de&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Al finalizar esta clase, serás capaz de:&lt;/em&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#al-finalizar-esta-clase-ser%c3%a1s-capaz-de&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1.&lt;/strong&gt; Identificar y utilizar el presente simple para describir hábitos, tradiciones y verdades generales en oraciones afirmativas y negativas, en preparación para hablar de ti mismo en entrevistas de trabajo y proporcionar información importante a tus clientes.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
