    <item>
      <title>Day 2 - Week 1</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-1/dia-2/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-1/dia-2/</guid>
      <description>&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-learning-objectives&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;🎯 Learning Objectives &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-learning-objectives&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At the end of the class, you will be able to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Master &lt;strong&gt;Simple Present&lt;/strong&gt; with &lt;em&gt;&amp;ldquo;to be&amp;rdquo;&lt;/em&gt; (am/is/are) and other verbs for descriptions, habits, and routines — in affirmative, negative, and question forms.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Use &lt;strong&gt;&amp;ldquo;to be&amp;rdquo; + adjectives&lt;/strong&gt; correctly to describe people and things.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Apply &lt;strong&gt;possessive adjectives&lt;/strong&gt; to show ownership properly.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-introduction&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;📖 Introduction &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-introduction&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Today you will describe people and things using &lt;strong&gt;adjectives&lt;/strong&gt; and the verb &lt;strong&gt;&amp;ldquo;to be&amp;rdquo;&lt;/strong&gt; correctly. You will talk about &lt;strong&gt;daily habits and truths&lt;/strong&gt; with other verbs. Finally, you will show ownership using &lt;strong&gt;possessives&lt;/strong&gt; for real-life conversations like work or family talk.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Day 2 - Week 1</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/elementary/semana-1/el-week1-day2/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/elementary/semana-1/el-week1-day2/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;temas-del-día&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Temas del día &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#temas-del-d%c3%ada&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to pray in English: FOR vs. TO&lt;/strong&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;The Alphabet&lt;/strong&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Verb&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;objetivos-del-aprendizaje&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Objetivos del aprendizaje: &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#objetivos-del-aprendizaje&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Al finalizar esta clase, serás capaz de:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Orar al iniciar cada clase, utilizando FOR + Sustantivos para agradecer, y TO + Verbos para pedir.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pronunciar el abecedario con los nombres correctos de cada letra, para deletrear tu propio nombre, nombres de tus clientes, nombres de ciudades, y otras palabras importantes en el idioma inglés.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Utilizar el alfabeto militar para que tus futuros clientes puedan reconocer una letra con facilidad a través de una llamada telefónica.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nombrar acciones que realizas tú u otras personas, reconociendo los verbos más comunes en el idioma inglés y pronunciándolos correctamente.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;introducción&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Introducción: &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#introducci%c3%b3n&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;El día de hoy, fortalecerás tres bases fundamentales para tu desarrollo en el idioma inglés. A través del vocabulario para orar, aprenderás a utilizar de forma básica “for” y “to”, evitando uno de los errores más comunes en niveles básicos ya que, aunque parecen similares, son usadas en contextos completamente diferentes. Dominar estas preposiciones te permitirá comunicar ideas con mayor precisión y claridad en contextos cotidianos.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Day 2 - Week 2</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-2/dia-2/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-2/dia-2/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;-learning-objectives&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;🎯 Learning Objectives &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-learning-objectives&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At the end of the class, you will be able to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Use &lt;strong&gt;Simple Past with &amp;ldquo;to be&amp;rdquo;&lt;/strong&gt; (was/were) in affirmative, negative, and question forms.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Use &lt;strong&gt;Simple Past with other verbs&lt;/strong&gt; (regular &amp;amp; irregular) for completed actions — affirmative, negative, interrogative, and short answers.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Focus on &lt;strong&gt;pronunciation&lt;/strong&gt; and use past tense for &lt;strong&gt;storytelling&lt;/strong&gt; and past events.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-introduction&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;📖 Introduction &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-introduction&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Today you will use the &lt;strong&gt;Simple Past tense&lt;/strong&gt; to talk about finished actions — &lt;em&gt;&amp;ldquo;I went yesterday.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/em&gt; As A1 students, use it for recapping weekend plans or sharing life experiences beyond present routines.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
