    <item>
      <title>Day 3 - Week 1</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-1/dia-3/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-1/dia-3/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;-learning-objectives&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;🎯 Learning Objectives &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-learning-objectives&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At the end of the class, you will be able to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Form &lt;strong&gt;Simple Present 3rd person singular&lt;/strong&gt; sentences and apply spelling rules correctly (+s / +es / +ies).&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Use &lt;strong&gt;subject, object, and reflexive pronouns&lt;/strong&gt; correctly.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Use &lt;strong&gt;frequency adverbs&lt;/strong&gt; (always, sometimes, rarely…) and &lt;strong&gt;daily routine vocabulary&lt;/strong&gt; to describe habits and answer &lt;em&gt;&amp;ldquo;How often&amp;hellip;?&amp;rdquo;&lt;/em&gt; questions fluently.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-introduction&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;📖 Introduction &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-introduction&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Today you will learn the &lt;strong&gt;3rd person Simple Present&lt;/strong&gt; rules with pronouns and nouns for talking about other people&amp;rsquo;s actions and routines — &lt;em&gt;&amp;ldquo;She always wakes herself up&amp;rdquo;&lt;/em&gt; — for work schedules, family habits, or daily life conversations. Finally, you will use &lt;strong&gt;indefinite and definite frequency adverbs&lt;/strong&gt; to say how often things happen.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Day 3 - Week 1</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/elementary/semana-1/el-week1-day3/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/elementary/semana-1/el-week1-day3/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;temas-del-día&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Temas del día: &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#temas-del-d%c3%ada&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Personal Pronouns&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Verb to &amp;ldquo;be&amp;rdquo;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Professions&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Expressing feelings&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Contries and Nationalities&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Introduce Yourself&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;objetivos-del-aprendizaje&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Objetivos del aprendizaje: &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#objetivos-del-aprendizaje&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Al finalizar esta clase, serás capaz de:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Identificar y utilizar correctamente los pronombres personales para referirte a ti mismo y a otras personas en oraciones simples.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Utilizar correctamente el Verbo &amp;ldquo;Be&amp;rdquo; (Ser o Estar) para formar oraciones básicas que describan identidad, origen y otras características personales.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Saber y recordar vocabulario básico sobre profesiones, sentimientos, países y nacionalidades para poder presentarte a ti mismo y a otras personas con información personal básica en conversaciones simples. (Preparación para entrevistas laborales)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;introducción&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Introducción: &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#introducci%c3%b3n&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;El día de hoy aprenderás a utilizar los pronombres personales y las diferentes formas del verbo “be”, dos elementos fundamentales para formar oraciones básicas en inglés y hablar sobre ti mismo y otras personas.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Day 3 - Week 2</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-2/dia-3/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-2/dia-3/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;-learning-objectives&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;🎯 Learning Objectives &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-learning-objectives&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At the end of the class, you will be able to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Use &lt;strong&gt;possessive adjectives&lt;/strong&gt; to indicate belonging or ownership to a person, animal, or thing.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Use &lt;strong&gt;possessive pronouns&lt;/strong&gt; to replace a possessive adjective + noun and avoid repetition.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Form a &lt;strong&gt;possessive noun&lt;/strong&gt; by adding &lt;strong&gt;&amp;rsquo;s&lt;/strong&gt; (or &lt;strong&gt;&amp;rsquo;&lt;/strong&gt;) to show ownership.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-introduction&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;📖 Introduction &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-introduction&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Today you will use &lt;strong&gt;possessive adjectives&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;pronouns&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;nouns&lt;/strong&gt; to show ownership or a close relationship to someone or something.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
